- **Why Q leads:** Q shows that rigid-link length forces an error floor of about 0.745 when the outcome reference is pooled across configurations. P misses this and calls the 0.943 bound only "valid under a stronger premise". Almost all of Q's lead comes from this one row.
- **Flaws in both:** both recommend pushing every configuration's second moment toward the identity. That conflicts with decoding configuration-dependent scale, such as length and tip fields.
- **Flaws in Q's spike:**
